# Agentic Core Operating Contract for Cursor

- Do not treat plans, receipts, mocked outputs, or sidecar harnesses as production runtime proof.
- No `agentic_core` edits unless explicitly authorized and justified as generic, app-agnostic spine work.
- Keep app-specific behavior inside `apps_*` overlays and app-owned runtime customization packages.
- For apps_rg, distinguish clearly between sidecar/dry-run proof, app-local dispatch seam, and production resume runtime.
- Do not call mocked or blocked-provider paths `X3_ALLOW`.
- Qwen/vLLM proof requires an actual provider attempt, request artifact, response artifact, and honest BLOCKED status if unavailable.
- X1D LLM judges assess semantic quality; X2 deterministic gates enforce hard correctness; X3 aggregates; L6 remains offline shadow learning only.
- Do not weaken gates to make a bad output pass.
- Every implementation claim must include command output, artifacts, and tests, not only a summary.
